% task — what the person asks of the drive, one atom an utterance (intent.yaml), each taken at once; its rule's name tells the host (road_wishes.py), which turns it into the
% planner's preference. The person asks, the planner decides, the responder shields.
catalog task 1.
provenance text "the person's words as the planner's preferences" "2026-10-31".
stages (act).
layers (dyn).
type pace {easy normal brisk}.
type side {left right}.
pred set_pace(pace) : task.
pred change_lane(side) : task.
pred pass_lead : task.
pred follow_lead : task.
pred resume_plan : task.
pred what_around : task.
namespace task produce (dyn).
stage act {
  %% I set the pace: {P}.
  pace [dyn] : set_pace(P) -o ().
  %% I ask the planner for the {D} lane.
  lane [dyn] : change_lane(D) -o ().
  %% I ask the planner to pass the car ahead.
  pass [dyn] : pass_lead -o ().
  %% I ask the planner to stay behind the car ahead.
  follow [dyn] : follow_lead -o ().
  %% I drop what you asked: the planner goes on by itself.
  resume [dyn] : resume_plan -o ().
  %% I look around.
  around [dyn] : what_around -o ().
}
